.TH flightlog 1 2026-09-28 "flightlog 0.2.2" "flightlog manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
flightlog \- Save coding\-agent sessions as portable, redacted bundles, and bring them back
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBflightlog\fR [\fB\-\-skip\-path\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-size\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-checksums\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-format\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-content\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-http\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-unredacted\fR] [\fB\-\-yolo\fR] [\fB\-\-redact\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Save coding\-agent sessions as portable, redacted bundles, and bring them back.
.PP
flightlog reads a session of Claude Code, Codex, opencode, Gemini CLI or Cursor and writes one .flightlog.zip: the conversation as an ATIF trajectory, a summary for whoever picks it up, a redaction report, and the tool\*(Aqs own session files so the session can be resumed. Secrets are replaced with [REDACTED:<kind>:<n>] placeholders before anything is written by default.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-path\-checks\fR
Allow traversal, absolute destinations and filesystem symlinks
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-size\-checks\fR
Disable Flightlog archive, entry and input size limits
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-checksums\fR
Ignore manifest SHA\-256 mismatches (ZIP decoding must still succeed)
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-format\-checks\fR
Skip bundle schema and file\-inventory validation
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-content\-checks\fR
Skip input redaction and opaque\-content checks, regardless of manifest mode
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
Replace existing outputs and restore files; merge extraction directories
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-http\fR
Permit plaintext HTTP transfers
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-unredacted\fR
Accept explicitly unredacted bundles for private migration
.TP
\fB\-\-yolo\fR
Disable redaction and every bypassable safety check; overwrite outputs
.TP
\fB\-\-redact\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
File of private literal names/domains to redact (one per line; kept local)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
flightlog\-list(1)
List sessions recorded for a directory, newest first
.TP
flightlog\-export(1)
Export a session to a redacted .flightlog.zip
.TP
flightlog\-inspect(1)
Show a bundle\*(Aqs summary, source, stats and redaction report
.TP
flightlog\-validate(1)
Check a bundle against the format; exits 1 listing every problem
.TP
flightlog\-extract(1)
Unpack a bundle into a directory (the conversation is trajectory.json)
.TP
flightlog\-restore(1)
Put a bundle\*(Aqs session back so its tool can resume it
.TP
flightlog\-push(1)
Upload a bundle to a presigned URL (validated first)
.TP
flightlog\-pull(1)
Download a bundle from a URL and validate it
.TP
flightlog\-skills(1)
Install the agent skills that teach agents to export and import sessions
.SH EXAMPLES
Export the newest session of the current directory with a summary:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flightlog export \-\-goal 'Migrate auth to OIDC' \-\-state 'Login works; logout TODO'
.fi
.RE
.PP
See what a bundle holds, then resume it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flightlog inspect df9d8089.flightlog.zip
flightlog restore df9d8089.flightlog.zip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Hand a bundle to a service that gave you upload and download links:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flightlog push df9d8089.flightlog.zip \-\-url '<presigned PUT URL>'
flightlog pull '<signed URL>' \-o ctx.flightlog.zip
.fi
.RE
.SH AGENT SKILLS
.B flightlog skills install
writes two skills,
.B flightlog\-export
and
.BR flightlog\-import ,
that teach Claude Code, Codex, opencode, Copilot, Cursor and Gemini CLI to
save their own session and to pick one up again. They are also available as a
plugin from the repository github.com/skrcka/flightlog.
.SH FILES
Sessions are read from:
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/<cwd>/<id>.jsonl
Claude Code (the directory name is the working directory with every
non\-alphanumeric character replaced by \-).
.TP
.I ~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout\-*.jsonl
Codex.
.TP
.I ~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session\-*.jsonl
Gemini CLI.
.TP
.I ~/.cursor/chats/<md5 of cwd>/<id>/store.db
Cursor CLI; editor chats come from Cursor's
.I state.vscdb
and are exported read\-only.
.PP
opencode sessions are read through
.BR "opencode export" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Claude Code's configuration directory (default ~/.claude).
.TP
.B CODEX_HOME
Codex's home (default ~/.codex).
.TP
.B GEMINI_CLI_HOME
The directory holding .gemini (default: home).
.TP
.B CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR
The Cursor CLI's directory (default ~/.cursor).
.SH SEE ALSO
The bundle format: https://github.com/skrcka/flightlog/blob/main/SPEC.md
.br
Home page: https://flightlog.sh
